# Global Clean Code Rules
- Use semantic English names. No abbreviations.
- Name by cause, not effect.
- Booleans: is/has/can/should/does prefix.
- Replace magic numbers with named constants.
- Prefer guard clauses (early return) over else.
- Avoid nested conditionals; keep logic flat.
- Comments must explain WHY, not WHAT.
